---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | Tarot Flower"
  description="How Tarot Flower handles contact messages, email signups, purchases, library access, analytics, cookies, and third-party services."
>
  <main class="privacy-page">
    <div class="privacy-inner">
      <header class="privacy-header">
        <p class="privacy-eyebrow">TAROT FLOWER</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="privacy-date">Effective 23 September 2026</p>
        <p>This policy explains what happens to personal information when you visit tarotflower.com, contact us, join an email list or waitlist, or buy and access an offering.</p>
      </header>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-contact">
        <h2 id="privacy-contact">Who to contact</h2>
        <p>Tarot Flower is operated by Vanessa Pokorny, who publishes as Vanessa Hylande. Postal address: 4285 Del Rio Rd., Atascadero, CA 93422, United States. For privacy questions or requests concerning this site, email <a href="mailto:vanessa@tarotflower.com">vanessa@tarotflower.com</a>. You can also use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-collection">
        <h2 id="privacy-collection">Information we receive</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Visits and security:</strong> The site is served through Cloudflare, which receives technical request information such as your IP address, browser, and requested pages to deliver and protect the site. Forms and library sign-in use Cloudflare Turnstile to deter automated abuse.</li>
          <li><strong>Messages and Oracle waitlist:</strong> The contact form asks for your name, email, and message. The Sacred Becoming Oracle waitlist uses that same contact system, with a required email-updates checkbox. Submissions are emailed to the Tarot Flower inbox; the message email also includes the submission time, IP address, and browser user-agent for abuse prevention.</li>
          <li><strong>Guide and email updates:</strong> The Goddess Embodiment Guide form asks for an email address, optional first name, and consent to receive the guide and occasional Tarot Flower emails. The email system stores your subscription status, the consent wording, time, source page, IP address, and browser user-agent in a Cloudflare database. It sends the guide and follow-up email through Google Workspace. Every such email can include an unsubscribe link.</li>
          <li><strong>Purchases and library access:</strong> Checkout takes place on Stripe, which collects payment details directly. For purchases that provide access to a Tarot Flower digital ritual, the site receives order information from Stripe and stores the purchaser’s email, Stripe transaction identifiers, amount, currency, and access entitlement in a Cloudflare database. The library also processes your email to send a sign-in link and stores hashed sign-in/session tokens and hashed rate-limit identifiers. Protected digital files are served from Cloudflare storage. Tarot Flower does not collect your full payment-card details on this website.</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics, only if you accept:</strong> Google Analytics 4 (measurement ID G-HZSXNP3G6Z) receives information about site use, such as pages visited and browser/device information, only after you opt in through the analytics choice. Google Analytics may then use first-party cookies such as <code>_ga</code> to recognize a browser. If you decline, the Google Analytics tag is not loaded.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-why">
        <h2 id="privacy-why">Why we use information</h2>
        <p>We use information to deliver the website, protect forms and accounts, answer messages, provide requested guides and updates, process orders, provide purchased access, and understand site use when you have accepted analytics. Where EU/EEA or UK data-protection law applies, the relevant bases are your consent for optional analytics and email updates; taking steps at your request or fulfilling a purchase; legitimate interests in site security and responding to inquiries; and applicable legal obligations for transaction records. You may withdraw consent for future processing at any time.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-storage">
        <h2 id="privacy-storage">Cookies and local storage</h2>
        <p>We store your analytics choice in your browser’s local storage as <code>tf_analytics_consent_v1</code>. If you accept analytics, Google Analytics may set its measurement cookies. Purchased-library access uses a secure, HTTP-only <code>tf_library_session</code> cookie with a maximum age of 30 days; it is needed to keep you signed in. Cloudflare security services may use cookies or similar signals when needed to verify visitors and protect the site.</p>
        <p>You can change or withdraw your analytics choice using <button type="button" class="privacy-choice-button" data-open-privacy-choices>Cookie settings</button>, also available in the footer. Declining analytics does not prevent you from reading the site, sending a message, or using purchased library access. You can also clear cookies and local storage in your browser; doing so may sign you out and reset your choice.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-services">
        <h2 id="privacy-services">Outside services and links</h2>
        <p>Cloudflare provides hosting, security, form processing, database and file storage. Google provides Analytics after consent, Google Workspace email delivery, and the fonts used on the site. Icons are loaded from the Cloudflare-hosted cdnjs service. Stripe operates external checkout pages and has its own <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>. Some older editorial articles contain YouTube videos, which load only if you choose to open them, and images hosted outside Tarot Flower, including legacy WordPress image hosts. When those resources load, their providers may receive request information. Social-media and other external links take you to services with their own privacy practices.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-sharing">
        <h2 id="privacy-sharing">Sharing and international processing</h2>
        <p>Information is shared with the service providers described above as needed to operate the site and its offerings, and when required by law. These providers may process information in countries outside your own, including the United States. Their processing and any applicable transfer protections are governed by their service terms and privacy documentation. To ask which safeguards apply to a particular transfer, or how to obtain a copy where available, email <a href="mailto:vanessa@tarotflower.com">vanessa@tarotflower.com</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-retention">
        <h2 id="privacy-retention">How long information is kept</h2>
        <p>Contact messages are kept as needed to respond and maintain relevant correspondence. Email subscription and consent records are kept while needed to send requested messages and document the choice; an unsubscribe record may be retained to respect the opt-out. Purchase and library records are kept while needed to provide ongoing access and meet applicable legal obligations. Security and analytics data follow the relevant service settings and operational needs. Single-use library sign-in links expire after 15 minutes, and library sessions have a 30-day maximum age; expired authentication records are cleaned up by the library service. You can ask about a specific record or request deletion where applicable.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-rights">
        <h2 id="privacy-rights">Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p>You can decline or withdraw analytics consent using Cookie settings, unsubscribe from email updates using the link in those messages, and contact us to request access, correction, deletion, restriction, or a copy of your personal information, as applicable. Where the law provides, you may also object to processing or complain to your local data-protection authority. To make a request, email <a href="mailto:vanessa@tarotflower.com">vanessa@tarotflower.com</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-dnt">
        <h2 id="privacy-dnt">Browser tracking signals</h2>
        <p>This site does not currently act on browser Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signals automatically. Google Analytics is off by default and loads only after an affirmative choice, which you can later withdraw. Third-party services may still receive technical request information when their fonts, icons, security checks, externally hosted images, or a video you choose to open are loaded, as described above.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-updates">
        <h2 id="privacy-updates">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>We will update this page if the site’s services or privacy practices change materially.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy-page { background: #f7f4ed; color: #253333; }
  .privacy-inner { width: min(100% - 2.5rem, 830px); margin: 0 auto; padding: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem) 0; }
  .privacy-header { margin-bottom: 3rem; padding-bottom: 2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #b9ab94; }
  .privacy-eyebrow { font: 400 .75rem/1.4 'Aboreto', serif; letter-spacing: .2em; color: #76614e; }
  .privacy-page h1, .privacy-page h2 { font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif; font-weight: 400; }
  .privacy-page h1 { margin: .4rem 0 1rem; font-size: clamp(2.9rem, 7vw, 4.5rem); line-height: 1.05; color: #14292a; }
  .privacy-page h2 { margin: 0 0 .65rem; font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.15rem); line-height: 1.16; color: #183638; }
  .privacy-page p, .privacy-page li { font: 400 1rem/1.8 'Quattrocento', Georgia, serif; }
  .privacy-page p { margin: .7rem 0; }
  .privacy-header > p:last-child { font-size: 1.12rem; }
  .privacy-header .privacy-date { color: #655d51; font-size: .88rem; }
  .privacy-page section { margin: 0 0 2.7rem; }
  .privacy-page ul { margin: .6rem 0; padding-left: 1.45rem; }
  .privacy-page li + li { margin-top: .7rem; }
  .privacy-page a, .privacy-choice-button { color: #6c4b31; text-underline-offset: .16em; }
  .privacy-page a:hover, .privacy-choice-button:hover { color: #8b3e35; }
  .privacy-page :focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #755b3e; outline-offset: 3px; }
  .privacy-page code { font-size: .9em; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .privacy-choice-button { padding: 0; border: 0; background: transparent; font: inherit; text-decoration: underline; cursor: pointer; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .privacy-inner { width: min(100% - 2rem, 830px); } }
</style>
